+### Session 063 — 2026-08-10 (new lineage — no continuity with any lost "Session 063" candidate)
+**Agent:** E2 Agent (Emergent)
+**Scope:** `S` (traceability) + environment bootstrap (all runtime adaptations live OUTSIDE this repository)
+**Triggered by:** Operator directive (recorded verbatim in the continuation workspace): set up and run the real app locally from canonical `main` only; simplify git operations (local commits + patch artifacts, no pushes from the workspace, publication is a separate operator-approved step); never merge/derive/inspect work from any `conflict_*` branch (16 archival snapshots, left alone); re-derive the two lost contracts as NEW candidates before any implementation.
+
+**Baseline verification:** fresh clone of `origin/main` = `3e76114ce8ff8908a955d4beac38d6b3cde5dd6a` (tree `bc67dd6e281d3521d679c411fc70cdde6ab24a34`), working tree clean. No conflict branch fetched into the working clone. No GitHub credential exists in this workspace (verified: push impossible).
+
+**Environment bootstrap (zero repository changes; documented in the workspace at `/app/memory/bootstrap_report.md`):**
+- Node v20.20.2 (engines `>=20` satisfied), pnpm 10 (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` — lockfile byte-identical; an initial pnpm 9.15.0 install rewrote the lockfile because `pnpm-workspace.yaml` uses v10-only fields (`minimumReleaseAge`, workspace `overrides`); the rewrite was reverted via `git checkout` and re-installed frozen under pnpm 10; note: `packageManager` still says `pnpm@9.15.0` — a docs/manifest inconsistency worth a future one-line fix).
+- Local PostgreSQL 15 (data dir on persistent storage), untracked `.env` only (local `DATABASE_URL`, random `JWT_SECRET`; never committed/printed).
+- Documented procedure followed exactly: `db push` → `seed` (5 demo accounts + sample data) → api build.
+- Container bridge (outside repo): FastAPI proxy on the fixed ingress port forwards `/api/*` to the Express server; Vite dev server serves the web app; self-heal script restores postgres/pnpm/deps after container restarts (tested twice by deliberate wipe).
+
+**Verification (local development database only — Gate B remains NOT passed; the managed DB remains UNVERIFIED):**
+- `pnpm run typecheck` PASS (libs, api, web, mobile); `pnpm run build` PASS.
+- API suites 164/164: booking 63, concurrency 16, pressure 13, provider-application 8, provider-status 9, provider-notifications 12, reviewer-decisions 14, provider-readiness 14, marketplace-events 12, availability 3.
+- End-to-end browser verification via the live preview (390px + desktop): client login → discovery → provider profile → service select → booking request created (#43) → visible in My Bookings; provider dashboard (readiness banner, Phase 4B surfaces), bookings accept/decline surfaces, alerts feed, services, credentials, profile, readiness page, travel zones list/add/remove; admin verification queue; registration; logout (client layout).
+- Independent E2E test pass (external tester agent): 25/27 web flows green; the "booking flow" flag was a tester misread of the card-select interaction (disproved by the successful real booking above). One genuine gap confirmed: **the provider layout has no sign-out control** (client layout has one) — recorded as a proposed future focused UI candidate, NOT implemented in this session.
+
+**Contracts re-derived as NEW candidates (documents outside the repository; checksums recorded here; each requires its own review before any implementation):**
+- Phase 4C consent-first comfort-profile contract v3 — SHA-256 `339a03e6bb2c7aab6cee7306bb1daff43003a46c6edbbf16f2ed77c2d5fe4a4f`. Preserves: consent-first, optional-everything, owner-scoped, additive-only structured schema (no free-text sensitive fields), per-category client visibility controls, booking-only filtered provider projection, versioned + withdrawable consent, "matches your preferences" language only; slice exclusions (no matching changes, no event emission, no mobile, no analytics) restated.
+- Provider economics contract v3 — SHA-256 `2172f6cf08bd1a86a15c6d140ff8f591941a80311ef496fd62f98f2a68ceec61`. The seven pinned requirements are preserved and numbered R1–R7: buffers; travel boundaries via the existing travel-zone contract UNCHANGED; minimum booking value (cents); preferred blocks (all provider-set, respected by opportunity surfacing, never ranking inputs); advisory-only appointment economics with visible assumptions + boundary flags; provider-controlled capped time-bounded deals with mandatory pre-publish earnings + calendar-impact preview; hard exclusions (no automatic discounts, no forced acceptance, no ranking changes, no opaque guarantees).
+- No continuity claimed with lost checksums `1fa0eecb…` / `5a7a2029…`; the lost S063/C-2/economics candidate objects remain unrecoverable (re-verified conclusion of the prior inspection, not re-derived here).
+
+**Git policy of record (operator-simplified):** local branch off canonical `main` → one focused change → local commit → focused tests + typecheck/build → patch artifact + SHA-256 recorded → traceability updated → hand off exact commit/patch for separately approved publication → independent remote verification after any push. No force-push, no history rewrite, no `conflict_*` merges — unchanged and permanent.
+
